.TH SYSTEMD-SENTRY 1 "September 2026" "systemd-sentry 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
systemd-sentry, sentry \- autonomous zero-trust system supervisor and triage engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B systemd-sentry
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.br
.B sentry
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B systemd-sentry
is an autonomous, zero-trust system supervisor written in 100% pure Rust for
.BR systemd (1)
environments. It provides sliding-window circuit breaking, intelligent root-cause
triage, flapping lockout protection, and guarded self-healing remediations.
.PP
The supervisor operates strictly under zero-trust principles: diagnostic engines
and AI models have zero shell access, zero command execution capability, and are
purely advisory. All automated actions must be explicitly whitelisted in
declarative policy configurations.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command-line help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-setup
Launch interactive configuration wizard.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B daemon
Run the background supervisor daemon. Reads configuration from
\fI/etc/systemd-sentry/config.toml\fR and policy files from
\fI/etc/systemd-sentry/policy.d/\fR.
.TP
.BR status " [\-\-json]"
Query the health status of the daemon and all tracked systemd services.
.TP
.BR check " [\-\-verbose]"
Validate configuration and policy drop-in files for syntax and semantic errors.
Exits 0 on success, or 78 (EX_CONFIG) on failure.
.TP
.BR triage " \fIUNIT\fR [\-\-json]"
Trigger immediate diagnostic root-cause analysis of a unit without waiting for
a failure transition.
.TP
.B monitor
Stream live failure events, circuit state transitions, and diagnostic reports
in real-time over the UNIX domain socket.
.TP
.BR incidents " [\-\-limit \fIN\fR]"
List recent diagnostic incident records (default limit: 20).
.TP
.BR inspect " \fIINCIDENT_ID\fR"
Display detailed diagnostic root-cause report, evidence, and logs for an incident.
.TP
.BR reset " \fIUNIT\fR"
Reset circuit breaker state, clear failure counters, and lift flapping lockouts
for the specified service unit. Requires superuser privileges.
.TP
.B mcp
Launch Model Context Protocol (MCP) server over standard input/output for AI
agent tools and IDE integrations.
.TP
.BR completions " \fISHELL\fR"
Generate shell completion script for \fIbash\fR, \fIzsh\fR, or \fIfish\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B systemd-sentry
uses standard BSD/Unix sysexits:
.TP
.B 0
Success (EX_OK).
.TP
.B 64
Command-line usage error (EX_USAGE).
.TP
.B 69
Required service or socket unavailable (EX_UNAVAILABLE).
.TP
.B 70
Internal software error (EX_SOFTWARE).
.TP
.B 74
Input/output error (EX_IOERR).
.TP
.B 77
Permission denied (EX_NOPERM).
.TP
.B 78
Configuration or policy validation error (EX_CONFIG).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/systemd-sentry/config.toml
Main daemon configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd-sentry/policy.toml
Base system remediation policy.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd-sentry/policy.d/*.toml
Drop-in policy override files merged in alphanumeric sort order.
.TP
.I /run/systemd-sentry/sentry.sock
UNIX domain IPC socket for client commands and monitoring.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd-sentry.conf (5),
.BR systemd-sentry.service (8),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
